# 5. DEFAULT TECH STACK

If no suitable stack already exists, use a modern full-stack TypeScript architecture.

Recommended default:

- Next.js
- TypeScript
- React
- Tailwind CSS
- SQLite for Phase 1 local database
- Prisma or another reliable ORM
- server-side API/actions
- secure password hashing
- database-backed or secure server-side sessions

Use current stable packages available in the environment.

Do NOT store passwords as plaintext.

Do NOT rely primarily on localStorage for important business data.

LocalStorage may be used only for harmless client preferences.

Important application data should live in SQLite/database storage.

Prefer simple maintainable architecture over unnecessary microservices.

This is an MVP.

Do not build NASA mission control for someone trying to hire a photographer.

