# 25. TWO-GATE DIGITAL HANDSHAKE SECURITY

Implement the proposed **two-gate QR handshake system**.

Purpose:

Protect:

- customer
- supplier
- escrow
- service completion

It functions similarly to confirmation between rider and customer in delivery/ride platforms.

---

# 26. GATE 1 — SERVICE START

At or near the event:

Generate a unique booking check-in token.

Display it as:

- QR code
- one-time numeric/alphanumeric code fallback

One party displays it.

The other verifies it.

Once verified:

```text
Booking:
CONFIRMED → IN_PROGRESS
```

Record:

- timestamp
- customer
- provider
- token verification
- booking ID

Token must become invalid after use.

---

# 27. GATE 2 — SERVICE COMPLETION

At the end of the service:

Generate a separate completion token.

Counterparty verifies it.

Once verified:

```text
IN_PROGRESS
↓
COMPLETION_PENDING
↓
COMPLETED
```

Then mock escrow is released.

Record an immutable-style local event log:

- booking
- actor
- timestamp
- event
- token verification

Allow fallback manual confirmation by an administrator in disputes.

